# Redirects, read by Cloudflare at deploy. One rule per line:
#   <from> <to> <status>
#
# /prices is hidden while the pricing model is being reworked. See SHOW_PRICING
# in site.config.js, which is what stops the page being built at all. This file
# is the other half: the address has been in the sitemap, in social bios and in
# every guide on the site, so somebody will still arrive at it. They get the
# contact page, where they can ask for the number instead of reading it.
#
# 302 rather than 301, and the difference matters. A 301 tells Google the page
# has moved permanently and to forget the old address, which is exactly wrong
# for a page coming back. A 302 says "not here for now" and leaves /prices free
# to be itself again the day SHOW_PRICING goes back to true, at which point
# these two lines are what to delete.
/prices /contact/ 302
/prices/* /contact/ 302
